{"base_rate":0.5336856010568032,"brier":0.16210501981505945,"bss":0.3486234012565562,"bss_hi":0.4491557785757305,"bss_lo":0.2521826756049733,"chart":{"base":[754.0,139.6],"fp":[249.1,254.0],"lead":"62,230.6 272,219.7 482,173.9 692,94.4","note":{"base":"skill 0.35 — higher than 59% of cities","fp":"low end +5pp, high end +17pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.3 °C — better than 31% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 5%; promised 100% → rained 87%"},"rel":"66.5,442.5 249.2,345.4 584.5,213.1 691.2,90.8"},"country":"NO","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.13084544253632752,"ess":352.2902172815655,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Trondheim</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Trondheim rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>87%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(1%), there is still roughly a <b>5%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nTRONDHEIM - VOLL, 3.6 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.35, ranked 55 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(27&ndash;91) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>5%</b></td><td class='num'>147</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>16%</td><td class='num'><b>24%</b></td><td class='num'>80</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>45%</td><td class='num'><b>32%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>74%</td><td class='num'><b>43%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>92%</td><td class='num'><b>74%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>87%</b></td><td class='num'>304</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Trondheim</b> <span class=\"muted\">NO</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.35</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>27&ndash;91\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>757 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Trondheim &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Trondheim\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" fo