"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"187.73844121532363\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"187.73844121532363\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"60.52857142857143,362.1904761904762 114.02050000000001,295.55 216.39108108108104,263.94594594594594 318.37631578947367,223.94736842105263 384.797894736842,113.78947368421052 411.5225657894737,65.89473684210526\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 1%&amp;#10;It rained 5% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 147 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"60.52857142857143\" cy=\"362.1904761904762\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 16%&amp;#10;It rained 24% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 80 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"114.02050000000001\" cy=\"295.55\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 45%&amp;#10;It rained 32% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"216.39108108108104\" cy=\"263.94594594594594\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 74%&amp;#10;It rained 43% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"318.37631578947367\" cy=\"223.94736842105263\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 92%&amp;#10;It rained 74% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"384.797894736842\" cy=\"113.78947368421052\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 87% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 304 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.5225657894737\" cy=\"65.89473684210526\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(53%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Trondheim the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.38) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.24).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>60%</td><td class='num'>0.241</td><td class='num'>14.0%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>61%</td><td class='num'>0.331</td><td class='num'>12.7%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>42%</td><td class='num'>0.368</td><td class='num'>12.1%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>50%</td><td class='num'>0.380</td><td class='num'>13.1%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":63.43049,"lon":10.39506,"n":757,"n_cities":134,"name":"Trondheim","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.06,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0071428571428571435,"n":147,"obs":0.05442176870748299,"sig":true},{"hi":0.2860000000000008,"lo":0.06,"mean":0.15825000000000003,"n":80